desc:Melody Phase
// A step-sequencer melody synth, sibling to Polyrhythm Phase.
//
// Up to 8 voices. Each voice plays a single note (a configurable
// number of semitones from the root) for its own Step Length, then
// hands off to the next active voice. Each voice also has a Note
// Length controlling how long its note actually rings — when Note
// Length exceeds Step Length, the voice's release continues in
// parallel with the next voice's attack (overlap / phrasing). When
// Note Length is less than Step Length, there's silence between
// voices (rest). When equal, clean sequential handoff.
//
// Rate is global. Step Length and Note Length per voice are
// expressed in cycles of the global rate, so you can write
// rhythmic relationships like "V1 = 2 cycles, V2 = 1 cycle,
// V3 = 0.5 cycles" and they'll line up.
//
// Inactive voices (Active = Off) are skipped in the sequence
// entirely. To insert a rest in the sequence, leave a voice
// Active but set its Note Length to 0 — the voice contributes
// silence for its Step Length, then hands off.
//
// Free reuse of Polyrhythm Phase's 10 waveforms, envelope shapes,
// binaural beat, and tuning math.
//
// CC0 — public domain.

// --- R20: THE RATE BLOCK. Exactly two controls, adjacent, in this order --
//     a rate value, then a rate mode of {BPM, Seconds, Hz, Every N beats,
//     N per beat}. Every rate in the suite carries this pair, and a plugin with
//     two rates carries two complete pairs -- the pan below has its own.
//
//     What used to be here instead, and why none of it survived: a `Host ratio`
//     picker sixty sliders from the mode that gave it meaning; then a
//     `Sync to host` switch, a `Host sync target` selector and a free
//     `Every N beats` slider. Both shapes had a control whose job was to write
//     into another control, which R20 forbids outright.
//
//     R21: the two host modes are RECIPROCALS and both are needed. Retiring the
//     old picker kept only the slow half, so eight cycles per beat had to be
//     entered as 0.125 -- an arithmetic step, which is the exact barrier this
//     suite exists to remove. The mode now picks which end of your music is
//     arithmetic-free. ---
// --- Rate (R20) and waveform ---
slider1:1<0.001,1000,0.001>Rate value
slider2:0<0,4,1{BPM,Seconds,Hz,Every N beats,N per beat}>Rate mode
slider3:0<0,13,1{Sine,Triangle,Saw,Golden TS,Golden SG,Golden GS,Bell,Wavefold,Half-sine,Phi-cascade,Phi Triangle,Phi Sine,Square,Pulse}>Waveform
slider4:25<1,99,0.1>Pulse width (%, 50 = square)
// --- Pitch. The mode is the plugin's; each voice has its note, its pitch
//     value and its fine tune. In Semitones the value is the MIDI note and
//     the note name binds to it both ways. ---
slider5:1<0,2,1{Hz,Semitones,Cents}>Pitch mode
slider6:2<0,2,1{Hz,Semitones,Cents}>Fine tune unit (for every voice)
slider7:440<20,2000,0.1>Tuning reference (Hz)
slider8:0<-12,12,1>Transpose (semitones)
slider9:0<-4,4,1>Octave shift
slider10:0<0,1000,0.001>Binaural beat (Hz, L/R offset)
// --- Envelope ---
slider11:10<0,100,0.1>Attack (% of note duration)
slider12:1<0,3,1{Linear,Cosine,Logarithmic,Exponential}>Attack shape
slider13:30<0,100,0.1>Release (% of note duration)
slider14:1<0,3,1{Linear,Cosine,Logarithmic,Exponential}>Release shape
// --- Glide ---
slider15:0<0,1000,0.001>Glide time (seconds; 0 = off)
slider16:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>Legato glide
// --- Pan ---
slider17:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>Pan enabled
slider18:2<0,15,1{Tremolo,Increment,Spread,Spread Reversed,Alternating,Alternating (Flipped),Distributed,Distributed (Flipped),Distributed (Ping-pong),Converging,Converging (Ping-pong),Diverging,Diverging (Ping-pong),Alternating every 2,Alternating every 4,Alternating every 8}>Pan mode
slider19:100<0,100,0.1>Pan spread (%)
slider20:10<0,1000,0.1>Pan glide ms (0 = instant)
slider21:8<2,1000,1>Cycle steps (per-cycle modes)
slider22:1<0.001,1000,0.001>Pan base rate (Tremolo / Increment modes)
slider23:0<0,4,1{BPM,Seconds,Hz,Every N beats,N per beat}>Pan rate mode
slider24:0<-1000,1000,0.001>Pan increment per voice (Increment mode)
// --- The sequence ---
slider25:0<0,8,1{All Active,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8}>Sequence length
slider26:0<0,5,1{Up,Down,Up-Down (repeat),Up-Down (no repeat),Down-Up (repeat),Down-Up (no repeat)}>Direction
slider27:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>Loop sequence

// --- Voices, seven controls each ---
slider28:60<0,127,1{C-1,C#-1,D-1,D#-1,E-1,F-1,F#-1,G-1,G#-1,A-1,A#-1,B-1,C0,C#0,D0,D#0,E0,F0,F#0,G0,G#0,A0,A#0,B0,C1,C#1,D1,D#1,E1,F1,F#1,G1,G#1,A1,A#1,B1,C2,C#2,D2,D#2,E2,F2,F#2,G2,G#2,A2,A#2,B2,C3,C#3,D3,D#3,E3,F3,F#3,G3,G#3,A3,A#3,B3,C4,C#4,D4,D#4,E4,F4,F#4,G4,G#4,A4,A#4,B4,C5,C#5,D5,D#5,E5,F5,F#5,G5,G#5,A5,A#5,B5,C6,C#6,D6,D#6,E6,F6,F#6,G6,G#6,A6,A#6,B6,C7,C#7,D7,D#7,E7,F7,F#7,G7,G#7,A7,A#7,B7,C8,C#8,D8,D#8,E8,F8,F#8,G8,G#8,A8,A#8,B8,C9,C#9,D9,D#9,E9,F9,F#9,G9}>V1 Note
